This repository contains both software and data. They are licensed separately.

## Software

The code in this repository (including `src/` and `.github/workflows/`) is
licensed under the MIT License. See `LICENSE-MIT`.

## Data and documentation

The data and documentation in this repository (including `target-data/`,
`auxiliary-data/`, `hub-config/`, and all README files) are licensed under
the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0).
See `LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0` or https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.

Under Section 3(a)(1)(A)(i) of CC BY 4.0, the following parties are
designated to receive attribution in any use of these data:

  - the Institut National de Santé Publique (INSP) and the Incident
    Management Support Team (IMST) of the Democratic Republic of the
    Congo, the source of the underlying surveillance data;
  - the Atlantic Coast Center for Infectious Disease Dynamics and
    Analytics (ACCIDDA) and the Kinshasa School of Public Health,
    University of Kinshasa, which processed the data for the BDBV
    Modeling Hub.

See "Citing these data" in README.md for the required attribution text.

## Model outputs

Files in `model-output/` are contributed by participating teams and are
licensed by each team under the license named in its file in
`model-metadata/`.
